# CineForge AI - project rules

Theme-driven, multi-agent cinematic short-video engine. Agents make creative and
planning decisions through typed artifacts; deterministic code handles budgets,
rights, state, timing, encoding and jobs.

Read first: [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) and [contracts](mdc:docs/architecture/contracts.md).

## Layout

- `apps/dashboard` - Next.js + TS + Tailwind (port 3000)
- `services/api` - FastAPI (port 8000), thin routes over the engine
- `services/worker` - RQ worker, queue `cineforge-agents`
- `services/media-worker` - RQ worker, queue `cineforge-media` (FFmpeg)
- `packages/engine` - Python package `cineforge`: contracts + domain logic
- `packages/schemas` - GENERATED JSON Schema + TS types (`make contracts`)
- `packages/prompts`, `packages/configurations` - prompts, themes, modes, prices
- `supabase/` - Postgres migrations + seed (Supabase CLI, port 54322)
- `infrastructure/docker`, `compose.yaml`, `Makefile` - local stack (`make help`)

## Contract freeze

Do NOT edit without the integrator: `packages/engine/src/cineforge/contracts/`,
`cineforge/config.py`, `runtime.py`, `db.py`, `configuration.py`, `testing.py`,
`supabase/migrations/`, `packages/configurations/`, `packages/schemas/`, root
`pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, root `package.json`, `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`,
`docs/architecture/`. Need a change? Stop and describe it.

## Ownership

Only edit files your workstream owns (table in AGENTS.md). Platform (A) owns
`infrastructure/`, `compose.yaml`, `Makefile`, `.github/`, `.dockerignore`,
`.cursor/rules/`, `scripts/` (not `export_contracts.py` / `generate_seed.py`),
`docs/development/`.

## Safety

- No binary media in Git (video, audio, images, renders). Only tiny approved
  fixtures under `tests/fixtures/approved/`. `make check-media` enforces it.
- No secrets in Git. Use `.env` (ignored); `.env.example` holds placeholders only.
  API keys go on the Sources page (Supabase Vault) or `.env`; `make check-media` fails on
  key-like strings.
- No paid API calls without explicit human approval. Defaults stay
  `PROVIDER_MODE=mock` and `ALLOW_PAID_PROVIDERS=false`; tests and CI never touch the
  network (`@pytest.mark.live` runs only with `RUN_LIVE_TESTS=1`). Paid runs only via
  `make demo-live` / `make test-live` after a human says so
  ([providers](mdc:docs/development/providers.md)).
- The stack has no login: ports bind to `127.0.0.1` only. Never expose it.
- No new dependencies without a stated reason (Python deps are locked by the integrator).
- Tests are mandatory. Every change ships with tests and the workstream's test command passes.

## Git

- Integration branch `phase0/foundation`. Never commit to `main`; it only gets reviewed PRs.
- One worktree per workstream: `git worktree add ../cineforge-ai-wt/<x> -b phase0/<x> phase0/foundation`.
- Small focused commits: `<area>: <imperative summary>`. Never force-push shared branches.
